+# tidyjson
+
+tidyjson reformats a JSON file and writes the result back to the same file.
+
+## Install
+
+From a clone of this repository:
+
+```sh
+npm install -g .
+```
+
+This puts the `tidyjson` command on your PATH.
+
+## Usage
+
+```sh
+tidyjson <file> [--indent N] [--sort-keys]
+```
+
+- `--indent N` sets the indentation width to N.
+- `--sort-keys` sorts object keys.
+
+tidyjson overwrites the file you pass. If the file is not valid JSON, it exits with code 2 and leaves the file unchanged.
+
+## Examples
+
+```sh
+tidyjson config.json --indent 2
+tidyjson data.json --indent 4 --sort-keys
+```
